  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A particle is placed at the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> of a frictionless track <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ABC</mi></math> as shown in figure. It is gently pushed towards right. The speed of the particle when it reaches the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> is: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo></math>Take <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"\"><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p><img src=\"assets\\qt0031_301f6cc7d9d5.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 147px;\"/>"
  },
